attribution: The Hanukkah hymn "Ma'oz Tzur" is a 13th-century Hebrew poem by an author known only as Mordechai; the tune is the Ashkenazi one, adapted from a German folk song and sung by German Jews since about 1450. First stanza. Both are anonymous and centuries old, so public domain.
